PickNotReleased.description:
No pick is published for the current product day. Each pick releases one hour before its kickoff, inside the operating window, 11:00 UTC to 23:00 America/New_York. A skipped day publishes nothing.

The body carries `error.code="not_found"`, `error.reason="pick_not_released"`, and `error.retry_at`. The response sets `Retry-After`. Both name the same instant, always in the future.

The instant is the earliest of:

- the next scheduled release, when a slot is selected;
- the next automatic selector attempt, about every 15 minutes, while the selector still scans the day and can add an earlier slot;
- the operating-window start, before 11:00 UTC or after a skipped day;
- about 60 seconds, when the schedule is absent, due, or a pick is overdue.

The value is advisory. An operator can publish a pick earlier. Schedule one request for the instant; do not poll.
